{
  "sutta_id": "SN4.13",
  "verses": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Linked Discourses 4.13",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 4.13"
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "Sakalika Sutta",
      "english": "The Stone Sliver"
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "See the introductory note to SN 1:38 ."
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I have heard that on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Rājagaha in the Maddakucchi Deer Reserve. Now at that time his foot had been pierced by a stone sliver. Excruciating were the bodily feelings that developed within him—painful, fierce, sharp, wracking, repellent, disagreeable—but he endured them mindful, alert, & unperturbed. Having had his outer robe folded in four and laid out, he lay down on his right side in the lion’s posture—with one foot placed on top of the other—mindful & alert."
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Then Māra the Evil One went to the Blessed One and recited this verse in his presence:"
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Are you lying there in a stupor,"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "or drunk on poetry?"
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Are your goals so very few?"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "All alone in a secluded lodging,"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "what is this dreamer, this sleepy-face?”"
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "The Buddha:"
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“I lie here,"
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "not in a stupor,"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "nor drunk on poetry."
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "My goal attained,"
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I am sorrow-free."
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "All alone in a secluded lodging,"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I lie down with sympathy"
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "for all beings."
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Even those pierced in the chest"
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "with an arrow,"
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "their hearts rapidly,"
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "rapidly"
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "beating:"
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "even they with their arrows"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "are able to sleep."
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "So why shouldn’t I,"
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "with my arrow removed?"
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I’m not awake with worry,"
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "nor afraid to sleep."
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Days & nights"
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "don’t oppress me."
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I see no threat of decline"
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "in any world at all."
    },
    {
      "number": 35,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "That’s why I sleep"
    },
    {
      "number": 36,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "with sympathy"
    },
    {
      "number": 37,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "for all beings.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 38,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Then Māra the Evil One—sad & dejected at realizing, “The Blessed One knows me; the One Well-Gone knows me”—vanished right there."
    }
  ]
}